<title>USA: Wisconsin Central employees choose unions.</title>
<headline>Wisconsin Central employees choose unions.</headline>
<dateline>ROSEMONT, Ill. 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wisconsin Central Transportation Corp said Sunday it was told by the National Mediation Board that locomotive engineers and conductors designated the Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers (BLE) and the United Transportation Union (UTU), respectively, to be their unions in three company units.</p>
<p>The units are Wisconsin Central Ltd, Fox Valley &amp; Western Ltd and Sault Ste. Marie Bridge Co, a news release issued by Wisconsin Central said.</p>
</text>
